{"id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#line","title":"line","path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.md","line":1064,"body":"","kind":"proof","status":"not_started","tex":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.tex#line","uses":["[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:busemann-function]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#rem:laplacian-weak-sense]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#prop:busemann-laplacian]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#thm:maximum-principle]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#thm:weak-harmonic-regularity]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:asymptotic-ray]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:asymptotic-ray-exists]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:asymptotic-ray]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:busemann-gradient-norm-one]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:function-bochner-formula]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#prop:parallel-gradient-splitting]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:busemann-along-line]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:busemann-pair-nonneg]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#cor:busemann-pair-vanishes-on-line]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.tex","label":"line","line":1700,"source":"\\label{line}\n\n\nA connected complete Riemannian manifold of non-negative Ricci\ncurvature that contains a minimizing line is isometric to\n$N\\times\\Ar$ for some Riemannian manifold $N$\n\\cite{CheegerGromoll2}.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\\sketch\n\\uses{def:busemann-function,rem:laplacian-weak-sense,prop:busemann-laplacian,thm:maximum-principle,thm:weak-harmonic-regularity,def:asymptotic-ray,lem:asymptotic-ray-exists,lem:asymptotic-ray,lem:busemann-gradient-norm-one,lem:function-bochner-formula,prop:parallel-gradient-splitting,lem:busemann-along-line,lem:busemann-pair-nonneg,cor:busemann-pair-vanishes-on-line}\nLet $B_\\pm$ be the Busemann functions of the two rays of the line.\nBoth are weakly superharmonic, while $B_++B_-\\ge0$ and vanishes on the\nline. The weak maximum principle applied to $-(B_++B_-)$ gives\n$B_-=-B_+$. Thus $B_+$ is weakly harmonic, hence smooth and harmonic by\nregularity. Through each $x$ there is an asymptotic ray, so\nLemma~\\ref{lem:busemann-gradient-norm-one} gives\n$|\\nabla B_+|=1$. Bochner's formula and $\\Ric\\ge0$ then imply\n$\\Hess(B_+)=0$. Proposition~\\ref{prop:parallel-gradient-splitting}\napplied to $B_+$ yields the product isometry.\n\\end{proof}\n\n\\begin{theorem}[Splitting Theorem]","html":" <p></p><span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c696e65\"></span> <p></p>A connected complete Riemannian manifold of non-negative Ricci curvature that contains a minimizing line is isometric to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$N\\times \\Ar $\">$N\\times \\Ar $</span> for some Riemannian manifold <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$N$\">$N$</span> <span class=\"reference\">\\cite{CheegerGromoll2}</span>.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p>\\sketch <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23def%3Abusemann-function\">↗ def:busemann-function</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh01_Preliminaries%23rem%3Alaplacian-weak-sense\">↗ rem:laplacian-weak-sense</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23prop%3Abusemann-laplacian\">↗ prop:busemann-laplacian</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23thm%3Amaximum-principle\">↗ thm:maximum-principle</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23thm%3Aweak-harmonic-regularity\">↗ thm:weak-harmonic-regularity</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23def%3Aasymptotic-ray\">↗ def:asymptotic-ray</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23lem%3Aasymptotic-ray-exists\">↗ lem:asymptotic-ray-exists</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23lem%3Aasymptotic-ray\">↗ lem:asymptotic-ray</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23lem%3Abusemann-gradient-norm-one\">↗ lem:busemann-gradient-norm-one</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23lem%3Afunction-bochner-formula\">↗ lem:function-bochner-formula</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23prop%3Aparallel-gradient-splitting\">↗ prop:parallel-gradient-splitting</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23lem%3Abusemann-along-line\">↗ lem:busemann-along-line</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23lem%3Abusemann-pair-nonneg\">↗ lem:busemann-pair-nonneg</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23cor%3Abusemann-pair-vanishes-on-line\">↗ cor:busemann-pair-vanishes-on-line</a> Let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$B_\\pm $\">$B_\\pm $</span> be the Busemann functions of the two rays of the line. Both are weakly superharmonic, while <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$B_++B_-\\ge 0$\">$B_++B_-\\ge 0$</span> and vanishes on the line. The weak maximum principle applied to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$-(B_++B_-)$\">$-(B_++B_-)$</span> gives <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$B_-=-B_+$\">$B_-=-B_+$</span>. Thus <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$B_+$\">$B_+$</span> is weakly harmonic, hence smooth and harmonic by regularity. Through each <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$x$\">$x$</span> there is an asymptotic ray, so Lemma <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23lem%3Abusemann-gradient-norm-one\" data-tex-node=\"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:busemann-gradient-norm-one\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a627573656d616e6e2d6772616469656e742d6e6f726d2d6f6e65\">2</a> gives <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$|\\nabla B_+|=1$\">$|\\nabla B_+|=1$</span>. Bochner’s formula and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\Ric \\ge 0$\">$\\Ric \\ge 0$</span> then imply <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\Hess (B_+)=0$\">$\\Hess (B_+)=0$</span>. Proposition <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23prop%3Aparallel-gradient-splitting\" data-tex-node=\"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#prop:parallel-gradient-splitting\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-70726f703a706172616c6c656c2d6772616469656e742d73706c697474696e67\">3</a> applied to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$B_+$\">$B_+$</span> yields the product isometry. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section> <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Theorem</div></section>[Splitting Theorem]","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:minimizing-line-implies-product","next":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#thm:splitting-theorem","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:busemann-function","title":"def:busemann-function","label":"def:busemann-function"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#rem:laplacian-weak-sense","title":"rem:laplacian-weak-sense","label":"rem:laplacian-weak-sense"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#prop:busemann-laplacian","title":"prop:busemann-laplacian","label":"prop:busemann-laplacian"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#thm:maximum-principle","title":"thm:maximum-principle","label":"thm:maximum-principle"},{"k